    ├── Used APIs  : KafkaProducer, send, flush, add_callback, add_errback
    ├── Pitfalls   : confluent-kafka uses librdkafka (C library) requiring system dependencies; confluent-kafka Producer.poll() 
    │   must be called periodically for callbacks to fire; the current callback-only pattern may need a poll loop; Different 
    │   configuration parameter names (e.g., 'bootstrap.servers' vs 'bootstrap_servers'); confluent-kafka defaults to asynchronous
    │   produce with delivery reports; error handling semantics differ slightly
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── The code uses kafka.KafkaProducer for synchronous message production with callback-based async handling. confluent-kafka 
        provides a compatible Producer API with similar send/flush semantics and callback support, making it a viable drop-in 
        replacement for the same synchronous producer role.

